Central product identity only (the equivalent of VS Code's product.json for VSCodium/Cursor):
Desktop productName/description, product-identity.cjs (display/pascal names, appId
ch.numezis.kletron*, MSIX id Numezis.*), Windows AppUserModelId, Tauri productName, `kletron`
alias console script, Linux desktop-entry APP_ID (= appId, hermes_cli/kletron_identity.py).
NOTICE (origin, MIT, non-affiliation).

Displayed strings are NOT patched. "Hermes" -> "Kletron" in CLI help, messages, logs, i18n
catalogs, window titles and the Desktop crash page is rewritten at BUILD time, in a throw-away
copy of the tree, by kletron/build/rebrand (rules.yaml + data-literals.txt, overlay). Upstream
tests run on the untouched source tree. Icons ride the upstream --icons flavor door
(kletron/brand/apps/desktop/{assets,public}).

Owner: Romain Magnin (Kletron)
Test: kletron/tests/py/test_identity.py; kletron/build/rebrand checks (kletron/build/build.sh)
Forwarded: not-needed (product identity of a downstream distribution)
Upstreamable: no
Budget: see kletron/tools/budget.py (target <= 40 contact lines)
Last-Update: 2026-11-05
